ProTracker/QTM effect information               © Steve Harrison, 1993-2023
---------------------------------------------------------------------------

The following 2 tables list the various effects available in ProTracker type
songs. Table 1 lists the standard effects (0-F), and table 2 lists the 'E'
commands/effects.

   Table 1 - standard ProTracker commands/effects
   ----------------------------------------------

   00 - Arpegio                         08 - <not used>
   01 - Pitch slide up                  09 - Set sample offset
   02 - Pitch slide down                0A - Volume slide
   03 - Tone portamento                 0B - Jump to sequence
   04 - Vibrato                         0C - Set volume
   05 - Tone portamento + volume slide  0D - Pattern break
   06 - Vibrato + volume slide          0E - Various, see table 2
   07 - Tremelo                         0F - Set speed / tempo


   Table 2 - 'E' commands/effects
   ------------------------------

 * E0 - Set filter                   ** E8 - <not used>
   E1 - Fine pitch slide up             E9 - Retrig note
   E2 - Fine pitch slide down           EA - Fine volume slide up
   E3 - Glissando control               EB - Fine volume slide down
   E4 - Set vibrato waveform            EC - Note cut
   E5 - Set fine tuning                 ED - Note delay
   E6 - Pattern loop                    EE - Pattern delay
   E7 - Set tremelo waveform            EF - Invert loop

 * The 'Set filter' command is used to turn on/off the Amiga's low-pass sound
filter. By default Amiga trackers switch the filter off, giving much better
sound quality - so this effect is *very* rarely used. RISC OS hardware does
not have a switchable filer, so this effect is ignored by QTM.

NOTE: early RISC OS hardware (Acorn Archimedes) had a fixed low-pass filter
which could only be disbled by a hardware mod, which is very worth doing (see
www.stardot.org.uk/forums/viewtopic.php?f=16&t=13630). Later RISC OS hardware
(A4 laptop, RiscPC, modern 32-bit RISC OS hardware) does not use such a harsh
filter, giving much better sound.
 
** The ProTracker 2.3D unused effect E8x has recently (well, 2016) been
assgined in ProTracker 2.3F to effect "Karplus-Strong synthesis", this may be
implemented in a future version of QTM.